        "name": "USN-3885-2",
        "description": "USN-3885-1 fixed vulnerabilities in OpenSSH. It was discovered that the fix for CVE-2019-6111 turned out to be incomplete. This update fixes the problem.  Original advisory details:   Harry Sintonen discovered multiple issues in the OpenSSH scp utility. If a  user or automated system were tricked into connecting to an untrusted  server, a remote attacker could possibly use these issues to write to  arbitrary files, change directory permissions, and spoof client output.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2019-6111"
